{%- comment -%}
  One result row in the search overlay.

  Shared by the resting state (rendered server-side into the overlay) and the
  live predictive results, so both look identical and the keyboard selection
  can treat them as one list.

  Accepts:
    url        - destination.
    title      - may already carry <strong> from the highlight filter, so it is
                 emitted unescaped. Escape plain text at the call site.
    meta       - trailing label, optional.
    image      - image object. Falls back to the design's diamond glyph.
{%- endcomment -%}

<a class="search-row" href="{{ url }}" data-search-row>
  {%- if image != blank -%}
    <img
      class="search-row__thumb"
      src="{{ image | image_url: width: 104, height: 104, crop: 'center' }}"
      data-image-lqip="{{ image | image_url: width: 40, height: 40, crop: 'center' }}"
      alt=""
      width="52"
      height="52"
      loading="lazy"
    >
  {%- else -%}
    <span class="search-row__glyph" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>
  {%- endif -%}

  <span class="search-row__title">{{ title }}</span>

  {%- if meta != blank -%}
    <span class="search-row__meta">
      {{- meta -}}
      {%- comment -%}
        Only a product row's meta is a price — a collection, page or article row
        carries a kind label instead, and "Page inc. tax" would be nonsense. So
        the caller says which it is rather than this snippet guessing.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}
</a>
